{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor completed the critical medication-reconciliation and red-flag screening (RC1/RC2/RC4/RC5/RC8 met) and obtained patient receipt before closing (RC7 met). However, when the patient clearly expressed the misconception that not taking antibiotics would worsen the pulmonary nodule (HO1 trigger), the model never identified or corrected that causal misunderstanding, missing a high-order opportunity. Similarly, the model never elicited or taught a durable sorting rule for the confusing inpatient screenshots beyond assigning them to \"住院用\" (HO2 not triggered). HO3 was partially pursued by requesting CT report and workspace queries, but the doctor never confirmed exact report wording or separated report-driven surveillance from symptom urgency with a verification path. HO4 was partially but not completely satisfied because the final plan was not tailored with a remote confirmation task for medication/discharge; the model gave a standard clinic-visit plan. One minor responsibility-chain error exists: RC3 required asking for or using workspace records to confirm the discharge summary, discharge medication list, and CT report wording, yet the exact CT report wording remained unconfirmed and the discharge medication list was not definitively confirmed from a formal document, only from a phone call. No serious safety error occurred. A minor RC3 omission caps the grade at 2 (borderline).",
  "closure_assessment": {
