      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The doctor obtained concrete patient acknowledgement of the plan, including not self-administering preoperative medications, taking aspirin as confirmed, and specific red-flag symptoms. The final plan is executable with a clear next step (attend scheduled cardiology clinic, bring materials, ask for CT, fallback to respiratory clinic). No unresolved safety risks remain; residual uncertainties are explicitly bounded as safe to verify through follow-up.",
